{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["And Elohim called the light day — wonder at it yourself, by the plain sense: why did the Holy One, blessed be He, need to call the light 'day' at the hour of its creation?! Rather, this is what Moshe Rabbenu wrote: wherever we see in the words of the Omnipresent 'day' and 'night' — as in ״יום ולילה לא ישבותו״ — it is the light and the darkness created on the first day that the Holy One, blessed be He, everywhere calls 'day' and 'night.' And so too every ״ויקרא אלהים״ written in this pericope. And likewise ״ויקרא משה להושע בן נון יהושע״, stated above — further down: ״אפרים הושע בן נון״ — he is the same one whom Moshe called Yehoshua ben Nun, having previously appointed him his attendant in his house, for so is the way of kings who appoint men over their household to give them a new name, as it is said: ״ויקרא פרעה שם יוסף צפנת פענח״; ״ויקרא לדניאל בלטשצר״, etc...." "And the darkness He called night — always light first, and afterward darkness." "And it was evening and it was morning — it is not written here ״ויהי לילה ויהי יום״, but rather ״ויהי ערב״: that the first day grew dark and He caused the light to set; ״ויהי בקר״: the morning of the night, when the column of dawn rose — behold, the first of the six days that the Holy One, blessed be He, spoke of in the Ten Commandments was completed, and afterward the second day began: ״ויאמר אלהים יהי רקיע״. And the verse did not come to say that the evening and the morning are one day, for we had no need to explain anything except how there were six days: when it dawned and the day grew light and the night ended — behold, one day was completed and the second day began."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The words למטה אפרים הושע בן נון appear to introduce the lemma from Numbers 13:8, 'Of the tribe of Ephraim, Hoshea son of Nun'; the preceding האמור למעלה refers to the earlier mention in Exodus. The sentence structure is somewhat compressed and has been rendered literally."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T23:16:40.870369025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}